From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:20:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 656/658] fix: [daveey] slim, gzipped transcript pages for the
 Desktop (hub opens reconciled in 1.3-2.5 s)

Five whys (live [open-timing], 2026-10-28): hub opens reconciled in
1.3-2.5 s, all of it waiting on GET /api/sessions/<id>/messages. The hub
answers in 10-50 ms, but a 120-row page of a long session was 1.4 MB
(495 KB, 235 KB for the others) and the reconcile time tracked page size
over the SSH tunnel (~0.8 MB/s). 528 KB was reasoning_details (provider
replay signatures, incompressible) and 212 KB reasoning_content repeating
reasoning; the Desktop never displays either when reasoning is present.
Nothing caught it because pages were only ever read over loopback before
remote gateways, and no test or log recorded page size.

- Server: with X-Hermes-Display-Transcript: 1, the messages route drops
  reasoning_details when reasoning is present and reasoning_content when it
  repeats reasoning, and gzips the page if the client accepts it. Other
  clients get the unchanged page. The same page: 1.4 MB -> 168 KB.
- Desktop: fetchJson marks transcript GETs with the header and
  Accept-Encoding: gzip, and gunzips; an older backend's plain page still
  decodes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
